WEBVTT

00:00:42.768 --> 00:00:45.896
- I'm surprised you didn't
call in sick this morning, Fry.

00:00:45.896 --> 00:00:47.856
Isn't it a special day?

00:00:47.856 --> 00:00:49.399
- No, just my birthday.

00:00:49.399 --> 00:00:53.195
All I want is to enjoy
the quiet desolation of space

00:00:53.195 --> 00:00:54.947
for a few peaceful hours.

00:00:55.697 --> 00:00:58.158
Surprise!

00:00:59.034 --> 00:01:01.411
- Uh, 'kay.
This really wasn't--

00:01:01.411 --> 00:01:03.664
- Happys birthdays!
- Happy whatchacallit!

00:01:03.664 --> 00:01:05.290
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.834
Happy B-day, Fry.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.170
- Jeez. How many people did you invite?

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.506
- Only a few. Less than 40.

00:01:12.506 --> 00:01:14.549
Surprise!

00:01:14.549 --> 00:01:16.385
Surprise, sailor.

00:01:16.385 --> 00:01:18.762
Thanks, everyone.

00:01:18.762 --> 00:01:20.263
- What's the matter, Fry?

00:01:20.263 --> 00:01:22.274
You look sick and so darn blue.

00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:24.518
- Chicken cordon bleu!? B'kaw!

00:01:24.518 --> 00:01:27.771
I don't wanna talk about it.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.025
Attention, party people.

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:35.529
We got a code 99.
Birthday boy unresponsive.

00:01:35.529 --> 00:01:36.780
- We need backup.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.992
So, I'ma turn the music back up.

00:01:45.747 --> 00:01:47.499
- Hey! Please, just--

00:01:50.794 --> 00:01:53.714
- Emergency!
All butts to battle cushions!

00:01:57.009 --> 00:01:58.635
We're being pulled off-course

00:01:58.635 --> 00:02:00.804
by some huge gravitational force!

00:02:00.804 --> 00:02:02.097
A black hole!

00:02:02.097 --> 00:02:03.348
dramatic sting

00:02:03.348 --> 00:02:05.058
- Scruffy begs to differ.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:07.019
I see it as more of a gray-brown,

00:02:07.019 --> 00:02:09.187
or perhaps toasted umber.

00:02:09.187 --> 00:02:10.731
- Impact in three!

00:02:10.731 --> 00:02:11.732
I mean, one!

00:02:18.947 --> 00:02:22.034
- Is everybody okay? 'Cause I'm not.

00:02:25.954 --> 00:02:27.873
Coming out!

00:02:27.873 --> 00:02:30.167
Ow!

00:02:41.386 --> 00:02:44.014
- We heard a girlish scream.
Are you okay?

00:02:44.014 --> 00:02:45.515
- Did anyone else see that?

00:02:45.515 --> 00:02:47.517
- No. I was busy making a tourniquet

00:02:47.517 --> 00:02:49.353
out of my tiny, tiny shirt.

00:02:49.353 --> 00:02:53.231
- What kind of hellhole has
Leela brought us to this time?

00:02:53.231 --> 00:02:55.984
- A barren wasteland devoid of life.

00:02:55.984 --> 00:02:58.236
Like Fire Island after Labor Day.

00:02:58.236 --> 00:03:00.113
There's literally nothing here.

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.366
Except that tasteless suburban teardown.

00:03:03.742 --> 00:03:07.079
That's the tasteless
suburban teardown I grew up in!

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:10.332
Whoa, weird.

00:03:10.332 --> 00:03:13.001
I was just repressing a memory of this.

00:03:13.001 --> 00:03:16.546
It's set up exactly like
my 8th birthday party.

00:03:16.546 --> 00:03:19.800
The theme was Game Night Afternoon.

00:03:24.972 --> 00:03:26.306
- What's wrong, son?

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:28.308
Worried about our boys in Grenada?

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:31.770
- No. It's just I-I'm not
very good at games, Dad.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.897
I don't wanna lose on my birthday.

00:03:33.897 --> 00:03:35.190
- Oh, don't worry.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.609
Not everything in life is about winning.

00:03:37.609 --> 00:03:40.404
But most things are.
Almost everything.

00:03:42.447 --> 00:03:45.284
Whoa! Happy birthday!

00:03:45.284 --> 00:03:46.868
- Here's Josh Gedgie!

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:48.578
High five, best bud!

00:03:49.079 --> 00:03:50.831
- Oh! So close!

00:03:54.376 --> 00:03:57.838
I can't believe it.
Everything is exactly how it was,

00:03:57.838 --> 00:04:00.590
right down to the two-liter bottle
of Dr. Peeper.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.676
- What kind of weirdos
would go to the trouble

00:04:02.676 --> 00:04:06.138
of recreating a low-budget
store brand birthday party?

00:04:06.138 --> 00:04:08.515
It was we!

00:04:10.017 --> 00:04:12.269
- He meant us. It was us!

00:04:12.269 --> 00:04:14.354
- I don't know.
I thought "we" sounded better.

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:15.981
- Look, never mind the grammar.

00:04:15.981 --> 00:04:18.567
How did you big-heads
get my old house here?

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:20.861
- I'ds likes to hears about the grammars.

00:04:20.861 --> 00:04:24.072
- Recreating Fry's house
was mere child's play,

00:04:24.072 --> 00:04:26.734
thanks to the power of our machine.
Behold!

00:04:29.244 --> 00:04:31.538
It scours the minds of visitors

00:04:31.538 --> 00:04:34.291
for powerful memories of conflict.

00:04:34.291 --> 00:04:36.668
- And recreates those conflicts

00:04:36.668 --> 00:04:38.462
in every detail!

00:04:38.462 --> 00:04:40.380
- Today, we shall reenact

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.342
Philip J. Fry's 8th birthday party,

00:04:43.342 --> 00:04:47.846
including all the thrilling
children's games he played!

00:04:47.846 --> 00:04:50.781
- I do enjoy Twister.

00:04:50.806 --> 00:04:54.269
- No Twister! You wouldn't believe
what the mean kids used to twist.

00:04:54.269 --> 00:04:56.897
- Then, we shall begin with the classic

00:04:56.897 --> 00:04:59.274
yet copyright-free game

00:04:59.274 --> 00:05:01.777
Barrel of Primates!

00:05:04.905 --> 00:05:07.199
- Who's ready to link monkey parts?

00:05:07.199 --> 00:05:08.367
I am! Me!

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:11.286
- They call me Monkey Breath for a reason.

00:05:11.286 --> 00:05:12.955
- Longest chain wins.

00:05:12.955 --> 00:05:15.791
Players, start your chains!

00:05:22.047 --> 00:05:25.008
- You shall play as two traditional teams

00:05:25.008 --> 00:05:26.885
of 17!

00:05:26.885 --> 00:05:29.513
- Only instead of boring plastic pieces,

00:05:29.513 --> 00:05:31.640
you shall be the primates.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.394
Kindly enter the barrels when ready.

00:05:40.023 --> 00:05:42.067
I'm ready now.

00:05:45.279 --> 00:05:48.282
- Let the game begin!

00:05:48.282 --> 00:05:50.033
- Uh, okay.

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:51.451
We should probably obey the heads.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.580
This is kind of fun.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.084
- Dang. You must work out a lot.

00:05:59.084 --> 00:06:02.087
- I'm a leg. Every day is leg day.

00:06:08.176 --> 00:06:11.930
- I don't remember this being
so hard when I was 8. Oh...

00:06:17.227 --> 00:06:19.896
- Did we mention there's a twist?

00:06:19.896 --> 00:06:23.066
I knew you were twist guys!

00:06:25.527 --> 00:06:27.738
- Oh, great. A pool of acid?

00:06:27.738 --> 00:06:30.157
- No. We're not monsters!

00:06:30.157 --> 00:06:33.785
- It's actually a highly alkaline liquid.

00:06:33.785 --> 00:06:34.995
That's the twist!

00:06:34.995 --> 00:06:37.581
It'll dissolve you twice as fast as acid!

00:06:37.581 --> 00:06:39.750
- But I have a fear of dissolving!

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.376
How do we get down from here?

00:06:41.376 --> 00:06:43.837
- By falling, of course.

00:06:45.047 --> 00:06:46.840
For in another twist,

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.676
these party games shall be...

00:06:49.676 --> 00:06:51.219
to the death!

00:06:51.219 --> 00:06:52.596
dramatic sting

00:06:52.596 --> 00:06:55.265
Although
we kinda guessed that from the bones.

00:06:59.436 --> 00:07:01.813
- Ooh, and it's a real barn-burner!

00:07:01.813 --> 00:07:03.523
Phil's the sentimental favorite,

00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:05.943
but the smart money's on four-eyes.

00:07:05.943 --> 00:07:08.695
- The name's Gedgie,
and it may look close,

00:07:08.695 --> 00:07:10.906
but I've got the Gedge.

00:07:12.699 --> 00:07:14.618
Fry's still in it!

00:07:14.618 --> 00:07:15.619
Ah-choo!

00:07:16.203 --> 00:07:17.704
- Look at him hook!

00:07:17.704 --> 00:07:20.791
- Impressive,
but my superior dexterity will--

00:07:20.791 --> 00:07:22.542
Aah!

00:07:24.044 --> 00:07:26.755
- I... w-won at something?

00:07:26.755 --> 00:07:29.633
I hope my grandma's
proud of me down in Hell.

00:07:29.633 --> 00:07:31.843
Nice job, Phil,

00:07:31.843 --> 00:07:34.471
but I'll Gedge you next time.

00:07:34.471 --> 00:07:36.473
That never gets old.

00:07:44.248 --> 00:07:47.084
- I say, I say,
I don't know how much longer

00:07:47.109 --> 00:07:49.820
these old hollow bird bones can hold out.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.947
- Why did you monsters dream this up?

00:07:51.947 --> 00:07:53.532
And are the streaming rights available?

00:07:53.532 --> 00:07:56.201
- Our motivations are three.

00:07:56.201 --> 00:07:58.036
Mine is to gain knowledge

00:07:58.036 --> 00:08:00.247
by making people crash on our planet

00:08:00.247 --> 00:08:03.542
and subjecting them
to bizarre experiments!

00:08:03.542 --> 00:08:06.878
- As for me, I don't have any motivations.

00:08:06.878 --> 00:08:09.715
- And I have two motivations!

00:08:09.715 --> 00:08:13.510
Gambling, and making these cool masks.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.722
Let the gambling begin!

00:08:16.722 --> 00:08:19.933
- Fifty quids on the red team.

00:08:19.933 --> 00:08:22.394
- A hundred quids on blue!

00:08:22.394 --> 00:08:24.271
Listen up, people!

00:08:24.271 --> 00:08:28.025
If we're going to survive,
we all need to work together!

00:08:28.025 --> 00:08:30.527
- Or we can shake the other team's bar

00:08:30.527 --> 00:08:32.654
and make those losers fall first!

00:08:32.654 --> 00:08:35.157
- I vote for the shaking thing.

00:08:40.078 --> 00:08:42.956
- Cut it out, Bender!
Cheating is against the rules!

00:08:42.956 --> 00:08:45.083
- There are no rules.

00:08:45.083 --> 00:08:46.543
Oh wait. Here are the rules.

00:08:48.462 --> 00:08:51.757
It just says, "Fun for ages 3 to 99."

00:08:51.757 --> 00:08:54.051
- No wonder I'm not enjoying it!

00:08:54.051 --> 00:08:56.345
- Now, hold on a minute.

00:08:56.345 --> 00:08:58.221
According to the laws of calculus,

00:08:58.221 --> 00:09:00.974
we might just be able to link chains

00:09:00.974 --> 00:09:03.810
to form a stable structure
known as a catenary.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.940
Damn! My dribbling
and differentiating arm!

00:09:13.695 --> 00:09:14.696
- Ah!

00:09:14.696 --> 00:09:17.950
- Is okay. Is only water.
Just as I foresaw.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.785
Oh. Oh, wait.

00:09:21.286 --> 00:09:24.957
Squid Game -esque vocalizing

00:09:30.963 --> 00:09:33.882
- That game was not fun!

00:09:33.882 --> 00:09:36.134
- Congratulations to the red team!

00:09:36.134 --> 00:09:39.137
I'm sure you'll all want to celebrate
with some birthday cake.

00:09:40.222 --> 00:09:43.225
- My parents and my grandmother
a-are dead!

00:09:44.685 --> 00:09:47.354
- I'm so sorry for your loss, Leela.

00:09:47.354 --> 00:09:48.814
Can I have their cake?

00:09:55.028 --> 00:09:56.947
- Where'd you get the snazzy candles?

00:09:56.947 --> 00:09:58.782
- Our machine made them!

00:09:58.782 --> 00:09:59.741
- Oh, right, right.

00:10:01.702 --> 00:10:05.163
The next game is a simple one.

00:10:05.163 --> 00:10:08.667
Fry must blow out all the candles

00:10:08.667 --> 00:10:11.086
in a single breath.

00:10:11.086 --> 00:10:12.254
- I can do that.

00:10:12.254 --> 00:10:14.506
- But, there's a twist.

00:10:14.506 --> 00:10:17.426
- I like a good twist.
That's what keeps the audience watching.

00:10:17.426 --> 00:10:21.138
- For each candle Fry doesn't blow out,

00:10:21.138 --> 00:10:25.100
the corresponding player will die!

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.768
- W-Wait, what, what, what?

00:10:26.768 --> 00:10:30.314
- Don't worry, guys.
I'm actually, like, really good at this.

00:10:34.234 --> 00:10:36.903
That's a lot of candles,
old man.

00:10:36.903 --> 00:10:38.071
You'll never do it.

00:10:44.244 --> 00:10:45.329
dramatic sting

00:10:52.169 --> 00:10:53.545
- Good going, brother!

00:10:55.255 --> 00:10:58.133
- Come on, gas bag! Blow your face off!

00:10:58.133 --> 00:11:01.053
- No fair! I got about 12 wicks!

00:11:05.849 --> 00:11:08.602
- Uh... look!

00:11:08.602 --> 00:11:10.479
He's still blowing somehow!

00:11:10.479 --> 00:11:11.939
It's going out!

00:11:15.567 --> 00:11:19.279
My only regret is not getting any cake!

00:11:22.282 --> 00:11:25.786
Pop Goes the Weasel playing

00:11:33.627 --> 00:11:34.836
- And the winner

00:11:34.836 --> 00:11:38.095
of the Tri-State Musical Chairs
Championship

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:40.873
is Philip J. Fry!

00:11:40.968 --> 00:11:43.470
Yay!

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:46.974
Pop Goes the Weasel continues

00:11:46.974 --> 00:11:49.726
It's been six hours.

00:11:49.726 --> 00:11:52.145
Can't you at least play
something a little catchier?

00:11:52.145 --> 00:11:55.565
- No. We have one song,
and we really like it.

00:11:59.945 --> 00:12:01.947
- Oh, breadcrumbs.

00:12:01.947 --> 00:12:04.408
- Nobody panic! Two to a seat!

00:12:04.408 --> 00:12:06.868
- You heard her! Start panicking! Ah!

00:12:08.912 --> 00:12:10.580
Oh! Oh!

00:12:16.169 --> 00:12:17.587
- Ow! Mom!

00:12:19.506 --> 00:12:21.258
- Ah! B'kaw!

00:12:43.363 --> 00:12:45.490
- Who likes piñatas?

00:12:52.831 --> 00:12:54.833
- Good try, Bartholomew.

00:12:54.833 --> 00:12:56.335
- No, it wasn't.

00:13:03.383 --> 00:13:05.761
That's impossible.

00:13:05.761 --> 00:13:08.096
It'd take all three Hulks to break that.

00:13:08.096 --> 00:13:10.891
Incredible, She, and Hogan.

00:13:14.144 --> 00:13:17.397
- That's the first time
I ever swung a bat and hit something!

00:13:20.984 --> 00:13:23.362
Since no one likes candy,

00:13:23.362 --> 00:13:26.657
we have filled our piñata with quids!

00:13:26.657 --> 00:13:27.908
- I like candy.

00:13:28.951 --> 00:13:32.204
My husband is dead!

00:13:32.204 --> 00:13:34.331
I can't go on!

00:13:34.331 --> 00:13:35.832
Okay.

00:13:37.751 --> 00:13:39.336
- That wasn't candy.

00:13:39.336 --> 00:13:41.338
- I didn't realize you were still alive.

00:13:43.215 --> 00:13:44.967
- Less yakking, more whacking!

00:13:48.553 --> 00:13:50.263
Oh! Ow...

00:13:50.263 --> 00:13:52.182
- Guys, I'm good at this.

00:13:52.182 --> 00:13:54.685
The secret is backswing...
- Ouch!

00:13:54.685 --> 00:13:56.270
- ...and follow-through.

00:13:59.523 --> 00:14:00.691
Whoop. Sorry.

00:14:03.068 --> 00:14:05.654
- I'm rich! Finally, I can give up limbo

00:14:05.654 --> 00:14:08.156
and start a professional sex league.

00:14:09.866 --> 00:14:11.868
Ah, hey, mon!

00:14:12.744 --> 00:14:15.289
- Oh no! My side piece!

00:14:17.499 --> 00:14:20.627
- And now for the penultimate game!

00:14:20.627 --> 00:14:23.672
- And then it will be over?
Th-This is the last game?

00:14:23.672 --> 00:14:26.675
- Penultimate means next to last.

00:14:26.675 --> 00:14:28.969
You lose the vocabulary game!

00:14:31.847 --> 00:14:34.349
- Kiffy! No!

00:14:37.352 --> 00:14:40.897
- This fiendish game
will be a treasure hunt

00:14:40.897 --> 00:14:43.900
for these orbs of horsehide!

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.486
- Blernsballs?
- No, baseballs.

00:14:46.486 --> 00:14:47.863
My mom had balls signed

00:14:47.863 --> 00:14:50.949
by her favorite members of the 1962 Mets.

00:14:50.949 --> 00:14:53.493
She hid them all over the house,
and we had to find them.

00:14:53.493 --> 00:14:55.078
- There are seven of you,

00:14:55.078 --> 00:14:58.665
but only four hidden baseballs!

00:14:58.665 --> 00:15:02.294
That's all we had.
And the machine can't make baseballs.

00:15:02.294 --> 00:15:04.338
It's not magic, for God's sake.

00:15:04.338 --> 00:15:07.132
- Let the hunt begin!

00:15:11.637 --> 00:15:14.806
I found a baseball
in the moldy tangerines!

00:15:14.806 --> 00:15:16.642
Ah-choo! Ah-choo!

00:15:16.642 --> 00:15:18.477
- One ball left, kids!

00:15:18.477 --> 00:15:20.062
And it's the grand prize,

00:15:20.062 --> 00:15:22.564
signed by Choo-Choo Coleman himself.

00:15:22.564 --> 00:15:25.567
- It's as good as Gedgie's.

00:15:34.952 --> 00:15:37.454
Don't bother.
I already checked the fridge.

00:15:37.454 --> 00:15:39.164
- Yeah, but things get lost in there.

00:15:39.164 --> 00:15:41.959
Just last night,
we had bicentennial meatloaf.

00:15:41.959 --> 00:15:44.836
Red, white, and green.

00:15:47.506 --> 00:15:48.715
A-ha!

00:15:49.424 --> 00:15:51.551
- Way to go, Phil!
- That's my boy!

00:15:51.551 --> 00:15:54.846
- B-B-But, I searched
every inch of that fridge.

00:15:54.846 --> 00:15:56.264
Fry must be cheating!

00:15:56.264 --> 00:15:59.268
- That would explain why
he's winning everything.

00:15:59.268 --> 00:16:01.937
- I am not a cheater! I'm not!

00:16:09.278 --> 00:16:12.239
- Come on, Fry. This was your house.

00:16:12.239 --> 00:16:15.492
Please tell me where the baseballs are.

00:16:15.492 --> 00:16:17.577
- You want me to cheat?

00:16:17.577 --> 00:16:19.037
I can't do that, Leela.

00:16:19.037 --> 00:16:22.332
I am not a cheater. I'm not.

00:16:22.332 --> 00:16:25.252
- Ooh, lookie-see what
I found in the crawlspace!

00:16:25.252 --> 00:16:27.963
Signed by both Bob Millers.

00:16:27.963 --> 00:16:29.923
There's only one left!

00:16:32.467 --> 00:16:34.094
Please, Fry!

00:16:34.094 --> 00:16:37.764
I know you don't wanna cheat,
but it's me. Leela!

00:16:37.764 --> 00:16:40.684
The woman you occasionally say you love.

00:16:40.684 --> 00:16:42.311
- I always love you, Leela,

00:16:42.311 --> 00:16:44.771
but there are two things I just can't do.

00:16:44.771 --> 00:16:47.357
Almost anything, and cheat.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:50.861
- You're right.

00:16:50.861 --> 00:16:53.780
You're sticking to
your principles.

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:56.325
I'm proud of you.

00:17:00.996 --> 00:17:04.082
- I've never cheated in my life. Never.

00:17:04.082 --> 00:17:06.251
But I'll do it. This once.

00:17:08.503 --> 00:17:10.714
- Well, he cheated.
You win that bet.

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:12.749
- Time to celebrate with a new mask!

00:17:15.844 --> 00:17:18.388
- Please remember me as a guy who never,

00:17:18.388 --> 00:17:21.391
ever cheated. Until now.

00:17:23.435 --> 00:17:27.064
- As the last orb has been found,
the hunt is over.

00:17:27.064 --> 00:17:28.732
Winners, step forward.

00:17:30.651 --> 00:17:33.070
You're not the winners.
Who said you were the winners?

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:35.364
- I forgot to mention the winners
are the ones

00:17:35.364 --> 00:17:37.950
who don't find the baseballs!

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.493
That's on me, guys.

00:17:44.957 --> 00:17:48.502
- Ooh. That was some impressive
reverse cheating, Fry.

00:17:48.502 --> 00:17:51.380
- For the last time, I'm not a cheater.

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.466
Just shut up, Gedgie.
I-I mean, Bendy.

00:17:54.466 --> 00:17:58.428
How dare you
mangle my blessed name!

00:17:58.428 --> 00:18:01.014
- Whoa, whoa! Save it for the finale.

00:18:01.014 --> 00:18:04.434
A game which will be played...
to the death!

00:18:05.769 --> 00:18:07.771
- They were all to the death!

00:18:10.607 --> 00:18:12.734
- The final game shall be a test

00:18:12.734 --> 00:18:14.820
of raw physical prowess!

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:16.655
Prepare yourselves

00:18:16.655 --> 00:18:20.492
for a brutal, no-holds-barred match of...

00:18:21.618 --> 00:18:24.579
Pin the Tail on the Donkey!

00:18:24.579 --> 00:18:27.457
- Aw, he's a cute little whatchacallit.

00:18:30.377 --> 00:18:32.087
Donkey.

00:18:32.087 --> 00:18:34.756
- The beast is clad in armor,

00:18:34.756 --> 00:18:38.593
save for this tiny area on its rear.

00:18:38.593 --> 00:18:40.804
- It is the donkey's Achilles butt.

00:18:40.804 --> 00:18:43.682
All its vital organs are clustered there.

00:18:43.682 --> 00:18:45.309
Just like me!

00:18:45.309 --> 00:18:47.978
Simply pin the tail on the butt

00:18:47.978 --> 00:18:51.356
to slay the donkey and claim victory.

00:18:51.356 --> 00:18:53.066
- I'm shivering with excitement

00:18:53.066 --> 00:18:54.985
because this game involves...

00:18:54.985 --> 00:18:56.987
masks!

00:19:03.285 --> 00:19:06.330
- Phil, Semitic kid,
it's down to you two.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.081
- Yes!
- Go, Gedgie!

00:19:08.081 --> 00:19:09.541
- Woo-hoo!

00:19:09.541 --> 00:19:12.461
- Yes! Everything's coming up Gedgie.

00:19:12.461 --> 00:19:14.713
Beat that, REO Cheatwagon.

00:19:16.882 --> 00:19:19.384
How's this for cheating?

00:19:24.848 --> 00:19:27.225
Oh, well. I guess you can't win 'em...

00:19:27.225 --> 00:19:28.769
dramatic sting

00:19:28.769 --> 00:19:31.313
...all?
- Look at my boy!

00:19:31.313 --> 00:19:34.441
You stabbed that donkey
like a professional donkey stabber!

00:19:35.484 --> 00:19:37.569
- I'm so proud of you.

00:19:37.569 --> 00:19:40.489
We'll go get your presents,
so you can open them.

00:19:40.489 --> 00:19:42.908
- Aw!
- This party sucks!

00:19:42.908 --> 00:19:45.035
- Told you Fry was a cheater.

00:19:45.035 --> 00:19:46.662
- Happy birthday, Fry.

00:19:46.662 --> 00:19:49.373
I hope you had fun cheating
'cause nobody else did!

00:19:55.128 --> 00:19:57.130
- But I didn't cheat!

00:20:00.008 --> 00:20:03.762
- I lost a best friend a long time ago
'cause he thought I was cheating,

00:20:03.762 --> 00:20:06.056
and I'm not gonna let it happen again.

00:20:06.056 --> 00:20:08.350
- I don't wanna lose you either, Fry.

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:11.353
- So I'm gonna prove I'm not cheating.

00:20:11.353 --> 00:20:13.772
Gouge out my eyes!
- Good idea!

00:20:13.772 --> 00:20:16.984
- Fry's suggestion is beyond horrific.

00:20:16.984 --> 00:20:20.612
Therefore, we shall do it!
- But, to make the game fair,

00:20:20.612 --> 00:20:23.365
we shall remove the eyes
of all the players!

00:20:23.365 --> 00:20:25.742
- Wait, hold on. What, what?
- Fear not.

00:20:25.742 --> 00:20:29.329
Our machine can remove eyes painlessly.

00:20:32.165 --> 00:20:34.293
Oops! Sorry. I stepped on your foot.

00:20:34.293 --> 00:20:36.670
It's okay. I'm fine.

00:20:37.337 --> 00:20:39.840
- Let the animal abuse begin!

00:20:42.676 --> 00:20:45.262
- Alright, you monster whosit.

00:20:45.262 --> 00:20:49.099
I'm gonna stick this doohickey
where the dealy don't whatsit.

00:20:53.312 --> 00:20:55.981
- I'm sorry I called you a cheater, buddy.

00:20:55.981 --> 00:20:57.983
Thanks, Bender.

00:20:57.983 --> 00:21:00.360
What do you say we team up
and go out fighting?

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:03.030
- I say, aw yeah, baby!

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.531
Friends to the end!

00:21:09.161 --> 00:21:11.330
My vital ass organs!

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:13.957
You are a cheater!

00:21:17.044 --> 00:21:18.879
- Bender? Bender?!

00:21:20.005 --> 00:21:23.300
- Congratulations, Philip J. Fry.

00:21:23.377 --> 00:21:25.129
You are the winner!

00:21:25.297 --> 00:21:28.305
- Return his eyes that he might gaze upon

00:21:28.305 --> 00:21:30.140
the horror he has wrought!

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:31.767
And the confetti.

00:21:47.908 --> 00:21:50.786
- Well, that's that.
I gotta get to church.

00:21:50.786 --> 00:21:53.664
- The games are now complete.

00:21:53.664 --> 00:21:56.875
The winner is... her. Whoever she is.

00:21:56.875 --> 00:22:00.128
We thank the players for their efforts.

00:22:06.009 --> 00:22:08.011
- How the shmeck are we alive?

00:22:08.011 --> 00:22:11.974
- The machine can easily
bring people back to life.

00:22:11.974 --> 00:22:13.850
Did I not mention that either?

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:15.435
- Farewell!

00:22:20.565 --> 00:22:24.528
- Well, that was the second
worst birthday party I ever had.

00:22:24.528 --> 00:22:28.156
All I ever wanted was for people
to believe I'm not a cheater.

00:22:28.156 --> 00:22:29.783
- We believe you, Fry.

00:22:29.783 --> 00:22:32.995
- Yeah, seeing as how that
old lady killed you so easy.

00:22:32.995 --> 00:22:35.539
- He went down like a sack of shoes.

00:22:35.539 --> 00:22:38.458
- I sure did. Thank you, everybody.

00:22:38.458 --> 00:22:40.961
- Group hug. Come on! Group hug!

00:22:51.054 --> 00:22:54.725
- Eh, you really think
a games party is a good idea?

00:22:54.725 --> 00:22:57.477
I mean, Phil's not much of a competitor.

00:22:57.477 --> 00:23:00.647
- Yeah, I know.
He still can't work a zipper.

00:23:00.647 --> 00:23:03.942
But, he's my son, and I love him,

00:23:03.942 --> 00:23:05.736
and I wanna give him a birthday

00:23:05.736 --> 00:23:09.239
that'll leave him feeling
like a winner for once.

00:23:38.977 --> 00:23:41.271
Mm, mm, mm

00:23:50.155 --> 00:23:53.241
I feel so dumb, dumb, dumb

00:23:53.241 --> 00:23:55.160
Mm, mm

00:23:56.620 --> 00:24:00.457
When I think about what you've become

00:24:00.457 --> 00:24:04.211
I feel sorry for your mum

00:24:04.211 --> 00:24:07.798
You say we're all having fun

00:24:07.798 --> 00:24:11.593
Do you know you're the only one?

00:24:11.593 --> 00:24:14.596
Dumb, dumb, dumb,
dumb, dumb, dumb

00:24:15.013 --> 00:24:18.016
Dumb, dumb, dumb,
dumb, dumb, dumb

00:24:18.558 --> 00:24:21.478
Dumb, dumb, dumb,
dumb, dumb, dumb

00:24:22.354 --> 00:24:24.773
Mm, mm, mm